<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan state governor bans porn channels.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan state governor bans porn channels.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The governor of a Venezuelan state said on Wednesday he had banned pornographic channels in his region.</p>
<p>Orlando Fernando, governor of the western Lara state, said he had based the decision on his obligation &quot;to defend morals and good habits.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;These channels promote the bad values of a perverse society...and we are not going to allow them on any account.&quot;</p>
<p>Several Venezuelan religious and political leaders have spoken out recently against pornographic channels, which have begun to be seen for the first time with the arrival of moderately priced satellite television.</p>
</text>
